        if you wish.  Thanks...



Installation: For a first time installation, Follow these steps:
~~~~~~~~~~~~
                1) Create a directory to contain all the data files.
                     Ex: makedir Doors:Pegged

                2) Create a dir inside the pegged directory named Players.
                     Ex: makedir Doors:Pegged/Players
                
                3) Make an assign to the directory you created above.
                     Ex: Assign Pegged: Doors:Pegged

                4) Copy all files to the Pegged: directory.

                5) Add Pegged in your doors section as an E! program.
                     -> Non Exclusive, IPL Value=0

                   That's it... Your done!  Enjoy and good luck ;-)

 
               Upgrading from Pegged 1.0:
               
                1) Create a dir inside the Pegged directory named Players.
                     Ex: makedir Pegged:Players

                2) Move all your player files into the Players directory.
                   Easy to do with a dir util like DOpus.
                   
                3) Copy the new level, youwin, and main files on top of the
                   old ones in the main Pegged: directory.



Playing The Game: Pegged is played by jumping a PEG across an adjacent PEG
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~  and placing it in an empty slot. Only Hoorizontal and
                  vertical jumps are allowed. The object is to jump all the
                  pegs until only one remains.

                  Jumped pegs are automaticaly removed from the board.

                  You receive bonus points for ending the game with the last
                  peg in the middle of the board.

                  - See the online docs for cursor movement instructs.



